## 680. Valid Palindrome II

## Approach: Two Pointers

I used the same two pointer approach as Valid Palindrome.

--  Start left from 0 and right from length - 1.
--  Compare both characters and move both pointers inward if they match.
--  If we find the first mismatch, we are allowed to delete one character.
--  So I try both possibilities:
--  Skip left → check left + 1 to right
--  Skip right → check left to right - 1
--  I use a helper isPalindrome() to check whether the remaining part is a palindrome.
--  If either side works, return true.

--  We don't actually delete anything from the string. We just move the pointer, so we don't need StringBuilder.

## Complexity
Time: O(n) — traverse the string and at most two extra palindrome checks.
Space: O(1) — no extra string or data structure.

Pattern: Two Pointers + One Allowed Deletion

SOLUTION :
class Solution {

    public boolean isPalindrome(String s, int left, int right) {
        while (left <= right) {
            if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) {
                return false;
            }
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        return true;
    }

    public boolean validPalindrome(String s) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = s.length() - 1;
        while (left <= right) {
            if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) {
                return isPalindrome(s, left + 1, right) || isPalindrome(s, left, right - 1);
            }
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
